From: bigjakk <6015188+bigjakk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: kcc: let X11 compositors unredirect the game window (KccX11AllowUnredirect)

Stock: X11Window::Initialize() (ui/ozone/platform/x11/x11_window.cc) sets
_NET_WM_BYPASS_COMPOSITOR = 2 ("never bypass") on every window it creates,
with the comment "Always composite Chromium windows if a compositing WM is
used ... this can lead to tearing of fullscreen videos".  That is the right
call for a browser playing video, and the wrong one for an uncapped game:
with a compositing window manager every frame is copied through the
compositor and shown on the compositor's own vsync, which adds up to about
one refresh interval of latency and makes --disable-gpu-vsync unable to
tear, fullscreen or not.

Change: with the feature enabled, ordinary top-level windows set the hint
to 1 ("prefer bypass") instead.  These keep the stock value 2:
  - every PlatformWindowType other than kWindow (kMenu, kPopup, kBubble,
    kTooltip, kDrag): they are small, often translucent or shaped, and sit
    on top of other windows;
  - any other override-redirect window (non-activatable windows, and
    windows whose X11ExtensionDelegate asks for override-redirect);
  - windows with an ARGB visual or created with
    PlatformWindowOpacity::kTranslucentWindow (Electron "transparent"
    windows): they need the compositor to blend;
  - the XEMBED status icon window.
The value is written once in Initialize(), exactly where stock writes it;
it is not changed on fullscreen transitions, so a borderless
monitor-sized window is treated the same as a real fullscreen one.

Gating: base::Feature KccX11AllowUnredirect, disabled by default, file
local.  With it off the property value is 2 for every window, as stock.
Browser process only.

What users will see with it on:
  - Tearing when vsync is off (that is the point), and lower input to
    photon latency.
  - A flicker or one-frame glitch when the compositor has to redirect the
    window again: a desktop notification, the client's own menu, tooltip
    or popup window, a volume OSD, or alt-tab appearing over the game.
  - On KWin/X11 desktop effects are suspended for the whole session while
    such a window exists (same as SDL games, which set this hint too).
  - Other top-level windows of the client (settings, devtools, splash) get
    the hint as well; a window made translucent after creation with
    setOpacity() or a shape still carries hint 1.

Who honours the hint (read from their sources, not tested here):
  - Mutter / GNOME on X11: reads it as on/off/auto.
  - KWin on X11: hint 1 suspends compositing while the window exists,
    unless "Allow applications to block compositing" is turned off.
  - xfwm4: unredirects a fullscreen, opaque, unshaped window only when the
    hint is 1 (so stock Chromium is never unredirected there).
  - picom: hint 1 forces unredirection of the screen while the window is
    mapped, but only when unredir-if-possible is enabled in its config.
  - No compositor (plain i3, openbox, ...): the hint means nothing, there
    is nothing to bypass.
  - XWayland: the Wayland compositor decides about direct scanout on its
    own; expect no effect.

A/B: run a compositing X11 session, fullscreen, with
  --ozone-platform=x11 --disable-gpu-vsync --disable-frame-rate-limit
with and without --enable-features=KccX11AllowUnredirect.  Check
  xprop -id <window> _NET_WM_BYPASS_COMPOSITOR   (1 vs 2)
then look for tearing above the refresh rate and measure click to photon
latency.  Open a menu and a desktop notification over the game to see how
bad the redirect flicker is on that compositor.

Not verified: nothing was compiled or run.  Compositor behaviour above is
from reading current upstream sources of each project, not from testing.

Platforms: Linux/X11 only (file is only built for the Ozone X11 platform).

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/x11/x11_window.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/x11/x11_window.cc
index 7f3275d01..abfb4a6cf 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/x11/x11_window.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/x11/x11_window.cc
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <vector>
 
 #include "base/compiler_specific.h"
+#include "base/feature_list.h"
 #include "base/memory/scoped_refptr.h"
 #include "base/nix/xdg_util.h"
 #include "base/no_destructor.h"
@@ -66,6 +67,11 @@ namespace {
 
 using mojom::DragOperation;
 
+// kcc: when enabled, ordinary opaque top-level windows set
+// _NET_WM_BYPASS_COMPOSITOR to 1 ("prefer bypass") instead of 2 ("never
+// bypass"), so a compositing window manager may unredirect them.
+BASE_FEATURE(kKccX11AllowUnredirect, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+
 // Opacity for drag widget windows.
 constexpr float kDragWidgetOpacity = .75f;
 
@@ -470,9 +476,21 @@ void X11Window::Initialize(PlatformWindowInitProperties properties) {
   // Always composite Chromium windows if a compositing WM is used.  Sometimes,
   // WMs will not composite fullscreen windows as an optimization, but this can
   // lead to tearing of fullscreen videos.
+  uint32_t bypass_compositor = 2;
+  // kcc: let the WM unredirect ordinary top-level windows instead.  Everything
+  // that only looks right when composited keeps the stock value: menus,
+  // popups, bubbles, tooltips, drag icons and other override-redirect
+  // windows, translucent (ARGB) windows and the embedded status icon.
+  if (base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kKccX11AllowUnredirect) &&
+      properties.type == PlatformWindowType::kWindow && !override_redirect_ &&
+      !visual_has_alpha_ &&
+      properties.opacity != PlatformWindowOpacity::kTranslucentWindow &&
+      properties.wm_role_name != kStatusIconWmRoleName) {
+    bypass_compositor = 1;
+  }
   connection_->SetProperty<uint32_t>(xwindow_,
                                      x11::GetAtom("_NET_WM_BYPASS_COMPOSITOR"),
-                                     x11::Atom::CARDINAL, 2);
+                                     x11::Atom::CARDINAL, bypass_compositor);
 
   if (properties.icon) {
     SetWindowIcons(gfx::ImageSkia(), *properties.icon);
